---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { cameraRegistry, belvidereFoiaLocations } from '../../../data/deflock';

const physical = cameraRegistry.filter(c => c.verification === 'confirmed');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Boone County & Belvidere Surveillance | NoRec.US"
  description="FOIA records, camera observations, Policy 450, retention, audits, and unresolved ALPR findings in Boone County and Belvidere, Illinois."
>
<main class="page_shell">
  <header class="article_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · BOONE COUNTY / BELVIDERE, ILLINOIS</p>
    <h1>Local ALPR systems, documented from the record.</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">Public records and field observations are presented separately. A mapped or photographed camera is not attributed to an agency unless ownership is established.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="evidence_box">
    <span class="status_label">EVIDENCE NOTE</span>
    <p>The archived camera registry contains 13 records assembled from physical scouting and third-party mapping. Agency ownership is unknown for most entries. Three Flock devices are marked physically confirmed. A separate City of Belvidere FOIA response lists seven city locations at the time of that record: six installed and one in planning.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">DOCUMENTED · BCSO POLICY 450</p>
    <h2>What the Boone County Sheriff's Office policy says.</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article><strong>Vehicle attributes</strong><p>The policy describes detection of plates together with vehicle make, model, color, and unique identifiers.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Search predicate</strong><p>The policy states reasonable suspicion or probable cause is not required before using an ALPR system itself during authorized operations; enforcement still requires an independent lawful basis.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Alert verification</strong><p>Officers are directed to verify alerts and vehicle information rather than treating an ALPR hit alone as sufficient enforcement justification.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Flock retention</strong><p>The policy states Flock-hosted data is purged after 30 days.</p></article>
      <article><strong>County retention</strong><p>ALPR data downloaded to the county server should be stored no longer than one year, subject to evidence and records-retention requirements.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Auditing</strong><p>The Sheriff or designee is to audit ALPR detection-browsing inquiries at least once per calendar year, including a random sample.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Auditable access</strong><p>The policy describes individual credentials and system use capable of being fully audited.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Immigration restriction</strong><p>The policy states data will not be shared by the county or its contractors/subcontractors for federal immigration-enforcement purposes involving specified federal immigration agencies.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="hero_actions">
      <a class="button button_dark" href="/archive/deflock/26-164_BCSO_Policy_450_ALPRs.pdf">Original policy PDF</a>
      <a class="button button_light" href="/archive/deflock/26-164_BCSO_Policy_450_ALPRs-ocr.pdf">OCR copy</a>
      <a class="button button_light" href="/archive/deflock/26-164_BCSO_FOIA.md">FOIA request record</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">CITY OF BELVIDERE · FOIA RESPONSE</p>
    <h2>Belvidere records list seven Flock locations.</h2>
    <p>The supplied response is a screenshot headed <strong>“FLOCK CAMERA LOCATIONS CITY OF BELVIDERE.”</strong> It shows “7 Total Locations” and an 86% complete indicator. Six entries are shown as installed and one as planning.</p>

    <div class="table_wrap">
      <table class="deflock_table">
        <thead><tr><th>Location name</th><th>Type</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {belvidereFoiaLocations.map(row => <tr><td>{row.name}</td><td>{row.type}</td><td>{row.status}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <figure class="foia_figure">
      <img src="/archive/deflock/Belvidere_Flock_Camera_Locations_FOIA_Response.png" alt="City of Belvidere Flock camera location response showing seven locations, six installed and one planning." />
      <figcaption>Archived image extracted from the supplied City of Belvidere FOIA-response DOCX.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="hero_actions">
      <a class="button button_dark" href="/archive/deflock/Belvidere_Flock_Camera_Locations_FOIA_Response.docx">Original DOCX</a>
      <a class="button button_light" href="/archive/deflock/Belvidere_Flock_Camera_Locations_FOIA_Response.png">Extracted image</a>
    </div>

    <div class="evidence_box evidence_unknown">
      <span class="status_label">CAUTION</span>
      <p>The response establishes the listed City of Belvidere locations at the time it was produced. It is not presented as a complete countywide ALPR inventory or as proof of ownership for separately observed cameras.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">FIELD / MAP REGISTRY</p>
    <h2>{cameraRegistry.length} working camera records, with ownership mostly unresolved.</h2>
    <p>The original registry contains a mix of Flock Safety, Motorola Solutions, and one unknown-vendor entry. Agency ownership is marked unknown across the working registry. That uncertainty is preserved here instead of being inferred from geography.</p>

    <div class="table_wrap">
      <table class="deflock_table compact">
        <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Vendor</th><th>Verification</th><th>Coordinates</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {cameraRegistry.map(c => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{c.id}</code></td>
              <td>{c.vendor}</td>
              <td>{c.verification === 'confirmed' ? 'Physically confirmed' : 'Unconfirmed / map-derived'}</td>
              <td>{c.latitude.toFixed(5)}, {c.longitude.toFixed(5)}</td>
              <td>{c.source}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p><strong>{physical.length} records</strong> are marked physically confirmed in the archived registry. That verification establishes the observed device/vendor at the recorded location; it does not independently establish public-agency ownership.</p>

    <a class="button button_light" href="/archive/deflock/Camera_Registry.md">Original camera registry</a>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">SUPPORTED / NOT SUPPORTED</p>
    <h2>What the records support — and what they do not.</h2>
    <div class="deflock_split">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">SUPPORTED</span>
        <ul>
          <li>The BCSO policy describes capture of more than the plate itself.</li>
          <li>The policy permits ALPR use without requiring reasonable suspicion or probable cause merely to operate/query the system in the authorized context described.</li>
          <li>Alert verification is required before enforcement action.</li>
          <li>Flock-hosted retention is described as 30 days.</li>
          <li>County-side downloaded data can remain up to one year under the policy, with exceptions for evidence/retention obligations.</li>
          <li>Annual browsing audits are required by policy.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">NOT ESTABLISHED</span>
        <ul>
          <li>That ICE has direct access for immigration enforcement; the supplied policy says the opposite for that purpose.</li>
          <li>That an officer may lawfully stop a vehicle solely because an ALPR alert occurred; the policy requires verification and a lawful basis.</li>
          <li>Which agencies currently receive Boone County ALPR data.</li>
          <li>How many users currently have system access.</li>
          <li>What the annual audits actually found.</li>
          <li>The ownership of most devices in the working camera registry.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="hero_actions">
      <a class="button button_light" href="/archive/deflock/Claims_vs_Evidence.md">Original Claims vs Evidence</a>
      <a class="button button_light" href="/archive/deflock/Verified_Findings.md">Original Verified Findings</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">UNRESOLVED</p>
    <h2>Not established by the published records.</h2>
    <ul class="about_questions">
      <li>Results of annual audits and any corrective actions.</li>
      <li>Current sharing and authorized-agency lists.</li>
      <li>Detection-browsing usage totals and access-log details.</li>
      <li>Authorized-user counts and training records.</li>
      <li>County retention schedules governing exported ALPR records.</li>
      <li>Current contracts, pricing, renewals, and grants.</li>
      <li>Installation dates and authoritative ownership for mapped devices.</li>
      <li>Regional or inter-agency search-access agreements.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
